Operator      Consumed    Produced            Description
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
dup           x           x x                 Duplicate top entry x [stack]
pop           x           -                   Remove top entry x from stack [stack]
xch           x y         y x                 Exchange x and y [stack]
cat           x y         xy                  Concatenation of x and y [string]
len           x           len(x)              Length of string x (bytes) [string]
lc            x           lc(x)               Lower case of x (ASCII) [string]
uc            x           uc(x)               Upper case of x (ASCII) [string]
rev           x           rev(x)              String reverse of x (bytes) [string]
rot13         x           rot13(x)            Rot13 encoding of x [string]
substr        x i k       x[i:i+k-1]          Substring of x starting at i (zero-based) of length k (as Perl) [string]
head          x k         x[0:k-1]            Initial part of string x, of length k [head,tail,skip,shed] [string]
tail          x k         x[#x-k:#x-1]        Trailing part of string x, of length k [head,tail,skip,shed] [string]
skip          x k         x[k:#x-1]           Trailing part of string x, skipping first k [head,tail,skip,shed] [string]
shed          x k         x[0:#x-k-1]         Leading part of string x, shedding last k [head,tail,skip,shed] [string]
strim         s nx ny     s'                  Trim nx bytes from the start and ny from the end of s [string]
ppl           x N         x'                  x right-padded with blanks to width N (left-aligned) [string]
ppr           x N         x'                  x left-padded with blanks to width N (right-aligned) [string]
zp            x N         x'                  x left zero-padded to width N [string]
nchar         x c         nc                  Number of occurrences of c in x (non-overlapping) [string]
catall        *           Stack-joined        Stringified stack [string]
joinall       * s         Stack-joined-by-s   Stringified stack with s as separator [string]
join          x y j       xjy                 Join two elements with string separator [string]
uie           x y         x-or-y              Use x if not empty (and not NA), otherwise use y [string]
urlec         x           urlec(x)            URL encoding of x (all but A-Z a-z 0-9 _ as %XX) [string]
urldc         x           urldc(x)            URL decoding of x (%XX) [string]
cgsum         c s         Sum of s in c       Sum of the lengths of the s operations in CIGAR c [string]
cgmax         c s         Max of s in c       Largest length of an s operation in CIGAR c [string]
cgcount       c s         Count of s in c     Number of s operations in CIGAR c [string]
md5           x           md5(x)              MD5 sum of x (hexadecimal) [string]
fmtall        f *         Map-*-into-f        In f replace # instances by stack (\# is a literal #) [string]
add           x y         x+y                 Add x and y [arithmetic]
sub           x y         x-y                 Subtract y from x [arithmetic]
mul           x y         x*y                 Multiply x and y [arithmetic]
div           x y         x/y                 Division (a float; by zero: inf or nan) [arithmetic]
idiv          x y         x // y              Integer division, floored (by zero: NA) [arithmetic]
mod           x y         x mod y             x modulo y, sign of y (by zero: NA) [arithmetic]
pow           x y         x**y                x raised to power y [arithmetic]
ipow          x y         x**y                x raised to power y in integers (negative y as pow; overflow: NA) [arithmetic]
max           x y         max(x,y)            Maximum of x and y [arithmetic]
min           x y         min(x,y)            Minimum of x and y [arithmetic]
neg           x           -x                  The sign-reversed value of x [arithmetic]
abs           x           abs(x)              Absolute value of x [arithmetic]
sign          x           sign(x)             The sign of x (-1, 0 or 1) [arithmetic]
sq            x           x^2                 Square of x [arithmetic]
incr          x           x++                 x incremented by one [arithmetic]
decr          x           x--                 x decremented by one [arithmetic]
rand          x           rand(x)             Random real in range [0, x) (x 0: [0, 1); see --seed) [arithmetic]
addall        *           sum(Stack)          Sum of all entries in stack [arithmetic]
mulall        *           product(Stack)      Product of all entries in stack [arithmetic]
maxall        *           max(Stack)          Max over all entries in stack [arithmetic]
minall        *           min(Stack)          Min over all entries in stack [arithmetic]
meanall       *           mean(Stack)         Mean of all entries in stack [arithmetic]
hmeanall      *           hmean(Stack)        Harmonic mean of the absolute values in stack [arithmetic]
gmeanall      *           gmean(Stack)        Geometric mean of the absolute values in stack [arithmetic]
int           x           int(x)              x truncated towards zero (do not use for rounding) [math]
floor         x           floor(x)            The floor of x [math]
ceil          x           ceil(x)             The ceil of x [math]
round         x           round(x)            The integer nearest to x, halves to even (2.5 -> 2, 3.5 -> 4) [math]
sqrt          x           sqrt(x)             Square root of x [math]
exp           x           e**x                Exponential function applied to x [math]
exp2          x           2^x                 2 to the power of x [math]
exp10         x           10^x                10 to the power of x [math]
log           x           log(x)              Natural logarithm of x [math]
log2          x           log2(x)             Logarithm of x in base 2 [math]
log10         x           log10(x)            Logarithm of x in base 10 [math]
sin           x           sin(x)              Sine of x [math]
cos           x           cos(x)              Cosine of x [math]
tan           x           tan(x)              Tangent of x [math]
dd            x N         x'                  x written with N decimal digits [precision]
sn            x N         x'                  x in scientific notation with N decimal digits [precision]
frac          x y N       x/y                 Fraction x/y with N decimal digits [precision]
pct           x y N       pct(x/y)            Percentage of x relative to y with N decimal digits [precision]
pml           x y N       pml(x/y)            Per mille of x relative to y with N decimal digits [precision]
map           x D         map-of-x            Value of x in dictionary D (not found: as D's default) [dictionary]
dord          x D         ord-of-x            Order of x in dictionary D (first appearance, 1-based; NA if absent) [dictionary]
ifelse        B x y       x or y              If B put x else put y (B: a non-zero number, or a non-empty string) [branch]
test          x y T       B                   Test T applied to x y: 1 or 0 (T a filter operator: /gt/ ~eq~ ~ ~isin~ ...) [branch]
save          x n         x                   Store x in register n (per row), x stays [state]
fetch         n           reg(n)              Value in register n (stored earlier in this row) [state]
rowno         -           x                   Current table row number (start one) [state]
r0wno         -           x                   Current table row number (start zero) [state]
lineno        -           x                   Current input line number [state]
now           -           t                   Current epoch (unix seconds) [time]
ttu           tu          s                   Time unit (3h, 1.5d; units s m h d w y) in seconds [time]
rttu          s           tu                  Integer seconds as days, hours, minutes, seconds (1d,2h,3m,4s) [time]
todate        u           date                Epoch as local date and time (%Y-%m-%d-%H-%M-%S) [time]
bitand        x y         x and y             Bitwise and of |x| and |y| [bit]
bitor         x y         x or y              Bitwise or of |x| and |y| [bit]
bitxor        x y         x xor y             Bitwise exclusive or of |x| and |y| [bit]
bitoff        x y         x rm y              Remove the bits of |y| from |x| [bit]
bitlsh        x y         x << y              Shift |x| left by |y| (overflow: NA) [bit]
bitrsh        x y         x >> y              Shift |x| right by |y| [bit]
tobin         x           x'                  Binary representation of x (negative: -101) [radix]
tohex         x           x'                  Hex representation of x (negative: -ff) [radix]
tooct         x           x'                  Octal representation of x (negative: -17) [radix]
binto         x           x'                  Read binary representation x (optional - and 0b) [radix]
hexto         x           x'                  Read hex representation x (optional - and 0x) [radix]
octto         x           x'                  Read octal representation x (optional - and 0o) [radix]
del           x p         x =~ s/p//          Delete pattern p in x [regex]
delg          x p         x =~ s/p//g         Globally delete pattern p in x [regex]
ed            x p s       x =~ s/p/s/         Substitute pattern p by s in x (s literal) [regex]
edg           x p s       x =~ s/p/s/g        Globally substitute pattern p by s in x (s literal) [regex]
get           x p         p-match-of-x        Group 1 of the match of p in x, or the entire match; empty if no match [regex]
npat          x p         np                  Number of (non-overlapping) matches of p in x [regex]
edbr          x p s       x =~ s/p/s/         As ed, $1 $2 .. (groups) and $0 (match) in s [regex]
edgbr         x p s       x =~ s/p/s/g        As edg, $1 $2 .. (groups) and $0 (match) in s [regex]
isforward     -           B                   1 if the alignment is on the forward strand, 0 if reverse (FLAG 0x10) [sam]
ref_len       -           n                   Length of the reference sequence (seqlen: @SQ or fasta) [sam]
ref_posx      -           p                   First reference position of the matched part (1-based) [sam]
ref_posy      -           p                   Last reference position of the matched part [sam]
qry_len       -           n                   Query length from the CIGAR (M I S = X) [sam]
qry_posx      -           p                   First query position of the matched part (1-based) [sam]
qry_posy      -           p                   Last query position of the matched part [sam]
ref_trail5p_N -           n                   Reference before the matched part (POS-1 + 5' trail) [sam]
ref_matched_N -           n                   Reference length of the matched part [sam]
ref_trail3p_N -           n                   Reference after the matched part [sam]
ref_trail5p_V -           n                   Reference length of the 5' trail of the CIGAR [sam]
ref_trail3p_V -           n                   Reference length of the 3' trail of the CIGAR [sam]
qry_trail5p_N -           n                   Query length of the 5' trail (S I) [sam]
qry_matched_N -           n                   Query length of the matched part [sam]
qry_trail3p_N -           n                   Query length of the 3' trail [sam]
aln_trail5p_cgr -           c                   The 5' trail of the CIGAR (leading S H D N I) [sam]
aln_matched_cgr -           c                   The matched part of the CIGAR [sam]
aln_trail3p_cgr -           c                   The 3' trail of the CIGAR [sam]
aln_nmatch    -           n                   M = X length of the matched part [sam]
aln_nedit     -           n                   Edit distance from NM:i (0 without NM) [sam]
aln_nmatchx   -           n                   NM minus the D and I of the matched part (mismatches) [sam]
qry_seq       -           seq                 Query sequence (SEQ, or filled for SEQ '*'; --sam-seqmiss) [sam]
qry_qual      -           qual                Query quality (QUAL, or filled with the sequence) [sam]
aln_ref       -           aln                 Alignment: reference line (needs --sam/FILE) [sam]
aln_aln       -           aln                 Alignment: match line (| x ~ - = _ `) [sam]
aln_qry       -           aln                 Alignment: query line [sam]
aln_rlr       -           aln                 Alignment: ruler with reference positions [sam]
aln_qlt       -           aln                 Alignment: query quality line [sam]
aln_all       -           aln                 Alignment: ruler, reference, match, query lines [sam]
aln_allq      -           aln                 Alignment: as aln_all, with the quality line [sam]
aln_all_pack  -           aln                 Alignment: as aln_all, lines joined by byte 0x01 [sam]
ref_trail5p   -           seq                 Reference before the matched part (needs --sam/FILE) [sam]
ref_matched   -           seq                 Reference of the matched part (needs --sam/FILE) [sam]
ref_trail3p   -           seq                 Reference after the matched part (needs --sam/FILE) [sam]
qry_trail5p   -           seq                 Query sequence of the 5' trail [sam]
qry_matched   -           seq                 Query sequence of the matched part [sam]
qry_trail3p   -           seq                 Query sequence of the 3' trail [sam]
sam_get       tag def     value               Value of optional field tag (XX:T, XX.T, XX-T), def if absent [sam]
/lt/          x y         x < y               Numeric less than [filter]
/le/          x y         x <= y              Numeric less than or equal [filter]
/eq/          x y         x == y              Numeric equal [filter]
/ge/          x y         x >= y              Numeric greater than or equal [filter]
/gt/          x y         x > y               Numeric greater than [filter]
/ne/          x y         x != y              Numeric not equal [filter]
~lt~          x y         x lt y              String (byte) less than [filter]
~le~          x y         x le y              String (byte) less than or equal [filter]
~eq~          x y         x eq y              String equal [filter]
~ge~          x y         x ge y              String (byte) greater than or equal [filter]
~gt~          x y         x gt y              String (byte) greater than [filter]
~ne~          x y         x ne y              String not equal [filter]
=             x y         x eq y              String equal [filter]
/=            x y         x ne y              String not equal [filter]
~             x p         x =~ p              Regex p matches x (:NAME: a fixed string) [filter]
/~            x p         x !~ p              Regex p does not match x [filter]
~isin~        x D         x in D              x is a key of dictionary D [filter]
~isnotin~     x D         x not in D          x is not a key of dictionary D [filter]
~hasval~      x D~v       D{x} eq v           x is a key of D with value v (not in test) [filter]
~hasnotval~   x D~v       D{x} ne v           x is not a key of D with value v (not in test) [filter]
/ep/          x y/e       |x-y| <= e          x within e of y (default e 0.0001) [filter]
/epx/         x y/e       |x-y| > e           x not within e of y [filter]
/om/          x y/k       x ~ y               |x| within a factor k of |y| (default k 2) [filter]
/omx/         x y/k       x !~ y              |x| not within a factor k of |y| [filter]
/all/         x m         all m in |x|        All bits of mask m set in |x| [filter]
/any/         x m         any m in |x|        At least one bit of mask m set in |x| [filter]
/notall/      x m         !all m in |x|       Not all bits of mask m set in |x| [filter]
/none/        x m         !any m in |x|       No bit of mask m set in |x| [filter]
/ISINT        x           B                   x is an integer (no VALUE; not in test) [filter]
/NOTINT       x           B                   x is not an integer (not in test) [filter]
/ISNUM        x           B                   x is a number, not nan (not in test) [filter]
/NOTNUM       x           B                   x is not a number (not in test) [filter]

